    <text>
    <body>
        
        <div type="letter">
            <div type="text">
                <opener>
                    <date>18 <formula><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></formula> 78—</date>
                    <salute>Dear Sir.</salute>
                </opener>
                <div type="transcription">
                     
                    <p>I am a great adorateur of the selection theory—but how is it possible, that there are hermaphrodits?<ref target="#foot.f1"/></p>
<p>Yours | Anthony Schobloch. <lb resp="#mjhawkins"/></p>
<p rend="left">Adr. Austria, Meran, Tyrol.</p> 
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="annotations">
                <note>Top of letter: ‘☿ Fool’ <hi rend="italic">blue crayon</hi></note>
            </div>
            
            
        </div>
        
        
        <div type="footnotes">
            <note xml:id="foot.f1">CD discussed hermaphroditism in both plants and animals; for plants, see <ref target="../bibliographies/bibl_6014.xml" resp="#mjhawkins"><hi rend="italic">Origin</hi></ref>, pp. 96–101, and <ref target="../bibliographies/bibl_7951.xml" resp="#mjhawkins"><hi rend="italic">Variation</hi></ref> 2: 131–40; for animals, see <ref target="../bibliographies/bibl_1966.xml" resp="#mjhawkins"><hi rend="italic">Descent</hi></ref> 1: 207–11.</note>
        </div>  
      
    </body>
